  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Keep Vision and Text Separate",
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "The expanded structure is one of 24 Vision blocks. Intermediate add2 outputs enter the next block; only the final block proceeds to post norm and spatial merge.",
        "Vision uses RoPE and ordinary residuals; text MLA uses NoPE and text Decoder sublayers use four-stream mHC.",
        "Spatial merge and the adapter do not force every image to 256 tokens. The processed grid determines visual row counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Data Granularity",
      "dot": "amber",
      "items": [
        "Logical structure only; DP vision sharding, dummy heads, and platform kernel choices are omitted.",
        "Visual embeddings are injected before the language backbone; there is no extra cross-attention in each text Decoder layer."
      ]
    }
  ]
